<h1>All Tracks</h1>
<p style="margin: 20px 0; color: #666;">
  Choose a track to begin your journey from mid-level to senior Rails developer.
  Each track contains multiple topics with overviews, exercises, checkpoints, and curated references.
</p>

<div class="track-grid">
  <% @tracks.each do |track| %>
    <div class="track-card">
      <a href="tracks/<%= track['key'] %>/index.html">
        <div style="font-size: 32px; margin-bottom: 10px;"><%= track['icon'] %></div>
        <h3><%= track['name'] %></h3>
        <p style="color: #666; font-size: 14px; margin: 10px 0;"><%= track['description'] %></p>
        <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
          <% depth = track['depth_target'] %>
          <% if depth.include?('Strong') %>
            <span class="badge badge-strong">Strong</span>
          <% elsif depth.include?('Working') %>
            <span class="badge badge-working">Working</span>
          <% else %>
            <span class="badge badge-exposure">Exposure</span>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>

<div class="content-section" style="margin-top: 40px;">
  <h2>📊 Coverage Summary</h2>
  <ul style="line-height: 2;">
    <li><strong>8 Tracks</strong> covering Rails internals, SQL, jobs, caching, observability, APIs, frontend, and architecture</li>
    <li><strong>41 Topics</strong> with detailed content (overview + exercise + checkpoint + references)</li>
    <li><strong>45-75 hours</strong> of estimated learning time</li>
    <li><strong>Three study routes:</strong> 12-week standard, 6-week fast track, or weekends-only</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <strong>Depth levels:</strong>
    <span class="badge badge-exposure">Exposure</span> Can define and recognize &nbsp;
    <span class="badge badge-working">Working</span> Can implement with notes &nbsp;
    <span class="badge badge-strong">Strong</span> Can design and debug in production
  </p>
</div>
